  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "世界古文明與當代社會",
    "sub_ename": "ANCIENT CIVILZATIONS OF THE WORLD AND PRESENT-DAY SOCIETIES",
    "describe_ch": "本課程為世界史前史與古文明的廣泛介紹，透過考古學研究探討更新世末期至歷史時代初期社會的發展，主題含人類演化史上的氣候變遷、狩獵採集者的全球性遷徙、動植物馴化與農業起源、文明的開展（城市生活、社會不平等、國家起源、貿易）、社會的崩壞與彈性調適等。透過本課程，學員將了解人類社會文化的多元發展，同時認知過去人類社會發展軌跡裡的重大轉折如何形塑現代社會，以及如何從過去的失敗經驗裡獲得對未來永續發展的啟發。",
    "describe_eh": "This course is a broad introduction to the prehistory humanity that uses archaeological theories and methods as a guide to survey the development of world human societies from the terminal stage of Pleistocene to the advent of writing. This global coverage of human prehistory examines ancient cultures and societies of Africa, Europe, Asia, Australia, and the Pacific. Topics covers the issues of climate change in human prehistory, hunter and gatherer diaspora, plant and animal domestication, agricultural revolution, the advent of civilization (the emergence of urban life, social inequality, origins of states, and trade), the collapse and resilience of past societies, and so forth. Through this course, students will gain an understanding of cultural diversity among past societies in the Old and the New Worlds, as well as an understanding of how the major transitions in the trajectory of past social development that shaped our modern society.",
    "pre_subname": "",
    "pre_sub_id3": null,
    "pre_sub_ename": "",
    "pre_describe": null,
    "pre_describe_en": null,
    "scr_credit": 2.0
  },
  "targets": [
    {
      "seq": 1,
      "describe_ch": "認識古代文明的興衰過程，認知過去人類社會發展軌跡裡的重大轉折如何形塑現代社會。",
      "describe_en": "To acquire knowledge on cultural diversity among past societies of the World."
    },
    {
      "seq": 2,
      "describe_ch": "如何從過去的經驗探討未來永續發展之策略。",
      "describe_en": "To understand how the major transitions in the trajectory of past social development that shaped our modern society, and of the inspiration of sustainable development from the aspects of past downfall."
    }
  ],
